### Growth batch G6 — public directory, world import, join log, console join, region transfer (2026-10-02)

Branch `feature/growth-g6-features-directory`. Everything customer-visible below is either read-only or
behind a default-OFF `Setting`; nothing here sends, charges or moves a VM.

**Public server directory (seo-025, seo-026, mkt-031).**
- Pure core `lib/server-directory.ts` (tests `test/server-directory.test.ts`), data side
  `lib/server-directory-data.ts`, page loader `app/nxm/_data/server-directory.ts`, template
  `tools/nxm/native/server-directory/*` (regenerate with `python3 tools/nxm/port_pages.py server-directory`;
  never hand-edit `app/nxm/_pages/server-directory/*`).
- Routes: `/servers` (free Minecraft, unchanged), `/game-servers/directory` (homepage: Featured shelf, a cover tile
  per game, best servers), `/game-servers/directory/<game>` (per game; fan-out `tools/nxm/routes/server-directory.json`,
  middleware pattern in `scripts/nxm-live-routes.ts`).
- Sources: opted-in paid servers (`Server.publicListing`), free Minecraft public servers, Nxeon community servers
  (`FreePublicServer`) and, only when enabled, `ExternalServer` rows ingested from the Steam list. Nxeon-hosted
  entries carry the Nxeon badge.
- **Dedupe rule.** A connection is a domain or an IP plus an optional port; a missing port is the game's default
  (`DEFAULT_PORT`), so `host`, `HOST.` and `host:25565` are one server. Entries also carry secondary keys (a
  hosted server's node ip:port) so a Steam-list row for a server we host collapses into our entry. Two ports on one
  IP are two servers. Survivor: Nxeon-hosted > has image > better described > newest; an external survivor inherits a
  missing image/description from its duplicates; an Nxeon entry is never edited by third-party data.
- **Order:** image first, then Nxeon-hosted, then busiest. Nobody can buy a position.
- **Indexing:** a game page is `noindex` and left out of the sitemap unless at least `INDEX_MIN_DESCRIBED` (3)
  described servers seen within 7 days back it. Owner links render `rel="ugc nofollow noopener"`.
- **Opt-in and moderation (mkt-031).** The opt-in is still the Public Directory card in Settings
  (`togglePublicListing`; switch off = gone immediately). The same card now takes an optional tagline, picture link
  and website link (`PublicListingMeta`, `lib/actions-listing.ts`). Picture and website are https-only and are NEVER
  rendered until an admin approves them in `/admin/directory`; editing either resets approval. Admin can also hide
  or feature a listing. IPs are never displayed for Nxeon-hosted entries. The card also gives a copy-and-paste kit
  for third-party lists (GameMonitoring, serverlist.gg): nothing is submitted on the owner's behalf.
- **Steam-list ingest (UNVERIFIED terms).** `scripts/directory-ingest.ts` (dry run by default; needs a free
  `STEAM_WEB_API_KEY`); `--apply` writes only while `Setting directory_ingest_enabled` is true, and rows only show
  publicly while `directory_external_show` is true (both toggled in `/admin/directory`, default off). The Valve
  server-list terms for republishing have not been read: do not enable until the owner has. Rows older than 3 days
  are pruned; no per-server probing happens on page render. Run at most daily (timer).
- Schema (additive): `PublicListingMeta`, `ExternalServer`, `DirectoryIngestRun`.

**Import my world (prd-013).** Panel Backups tab, `components/customer/gamepanel/GameWorldImport.tsx`; rules in
`lib/world-import.ts` (tests), server half `lib/actions-world-import.ts`. Valheim: `.db`+`.fwl` pair (or world
folder) into `worlds_local`, then `world` is switched and the server restarts; a new name never touches the running
world. Minecraft: a folder containing `level.dat` (plus `_nether`/`_the_end`) replaces the current level folder.
Terraria: one `.wld` replaces the current world file. A `.zip` is unpacked with `extractArchive`. Uploads reuse
`/api/files` (250 MB per file); the authoritative check runs on what really landed in a staging folder
(`.nxeon-import-<id>`); anything replaced is renamed `<name>.pre-import-<stamp>`, never deleted; failure rolls back.
A replacing import is refused while the game may be running (stop it first).

**Recent joins card (prd-014).** `GameJoinLog` on Overview (real `PlayerSession` rows via `getPlayerHistory`) for
families in `lib/game-player-tracking.ts` (test pins it to the worker): RCON families and log-tailed Valheim and
Rust. Rust is new: `GAME_LOG_TRACKING.rust` reads `<ip>:<port>/<steamid>/<name> joined [` and `... disconnecting:`
lines; only the name is stored; leaves are observed (not inferred). The Rust format is NOT yet verified against a
live Nxeon Rust server. The log tail is capped at 500 lines per sweep, so a very chatty Rust log can miss events.

**Console-join instructions (prd-015).** `lib/console-join.ts` (tests) generates per-server steps from the saved
settings for Palworld (Community Servers browser, exact Server Name, `community-servers` must be on) and Valheim
(`CROSSPLAY` on; find by name or join code, read from the server log on request). Shown as the "Console players"
import { cleanText, connKey, isIpv4, normalizeHost } from "@/lib/server-directory";

/**
 * Steam master-server list -> directory candidates. PURE parsing + a thin
 * fetcher; the database half is lib/directory-ingest/run.ts.
 *
 * Source: Steam Web API `IGameServersService/GetServerList` (needs a free Steam
 * Web API key in STEAM_WEB_API_KEY). Its terms for republishing the list on a
 * public directory are UNVERIFIED (growth item seo-026) — which is why nothing
 * here runs unless an admin turned ingestion on, and why the fetcher is only
 * ever called by scripts/directory-ingest.ts, never from a page render.
 *
 * Response rows (the documented fields we use): addr "ip:queryPort",
 * gameport, name, appid, gamedir, version, region, players, max_players, bots,
 * map, secure, dedicated, os, gametype (comma-separated tags). Anything else
 * is ignored; anything missing stays empty — nothing is invented.
 */

/** Families that register on the Steam master list, with their Steam app ids. */
export const VALVE_APPIDS: Record<string, number> = {
  valheim: 892970,
  projectzomboid: 108600,
  rust: 252490,
  cs2: 730,
  tf2: 440,
  gmod: 4000,
  l4d2: 550,
  ark: 346110,
  unturned: 304930,
  sdtd: 251570,
  conan: 440900,
};

export type ValveRaw = {
  addr?: string; gameport?: number; name?: string; appid?: number; version?: string;
  players?: number; max_players?: number; bots?: number; map?: string; dedicated?: boolean; gametype?: string;
};

export type ExternalCandidate = {
  source: "valve";
  sourceKey: string;
  game: string;
  name: string;
  host: string;
  ip: string;
  port: number;
  queryPort: number | null;
  map: string | null;
  players: number | null;
  maxPlayers: number | null;
  version: string | null;
  tags: string[];
  connKey: string;
  ipKey: string;
};

const num = (v: unknown): number | null => (typeof v === "number" && Number.isFinite(v) && v >= 0 ? Math.floor(v) : null);

/** Server names come from strangers: strip controls, collapse space, bound length, drop empties/links-only. */
export function cleanServerName(raw: unknown): string | null {
  const t = cleanText(raw, 80);
  if (!t || t.length < 3) return null;
  if (!/[\p{L}\p{N}]/u.test(t)) return null;
  return t;
}

export function parseValveRow(game: string, r: ValveRaw): ExternalCandidate | null {
  const m = /^(\d{1,3}(?:\.\d{1,3}){3}):(\d{1,5})$/.exec(String(r.addr ?? ""));
  if (!m) return null;
  const ip = normalizeHost(m[1]);
  if (!isIpv4(ip) || /^(0\.|10\.|127\.|169\.254\.|192\.168\.|172\.(1[6-9]|2\d|3[01])\.)/.test(ip)) return null;
  const queryPort = Number(m[2]);
  // The join port is `gameport` when the row reports one; otherwise the address port.
  const port = num(r.gameport) && num(r.gameport)! > 0 && num(r.gameport)! < 65536 ? num(r.gameport)! : queryPort;
  if (!(port >= 1 && port <= 65535)) return null;
  const name = cleanServerName(r.name);
  if (!name) return null;
  if (r.dedicated === false) return null;
  const tags = String(r.gametype ?? "").split(",").map((t) => cleanText(t, 24)).filter((t): t is string => !!t).slice(0, 8);
  const key = connKey(game, ip, port);
  return {
    source: "valve", sourceKey: `${ip}:${port}`, game, name, host: ip, ip, port,
    queryPort: queryPort !== port ? queryPort : null,
    map: cleanText(r.map, 40), players: num(r.players), maxPlayers: num(r.max_players),
    version: cleanText(r.version, 24), tags, connKey: key, ipKey: key,
  };
}

export function parseValveResponse(game: string, json: unknown): ExternalCandidate[] {
  const rows = (json as { response?: { servers?: ValveRaw[] } } | null)?.response?.servers;
  if (!Array.isArray(rows)) return [];
  const seen = new Set<string>();
  const out: ExternalCandidate[] = [];
  for (const r of rows) {
    const c = parseValveRow(game, r);
    if (!c || seen.has(c.sourceKey)) continue;
    seen.add(c.sourceKey);
    out.push(c);
  }
  return out;
}

export class ValveFetchError extends Error {}

/** One bounded request. Throws ValveFetchError on anything but a clean 200 JSON body. */
export async function fetchValveList(game: string, opts: { key: string; limit?: number; timeoutMs?: number; fetchImpl?: typeof fetch }): Promise<ExternalCandidate[]> {
  const appid = VALVE_APPIDS[game];
  if (!appid) throw new ValveFetchError(`No Steam app id known for ${game}`);
  const limit = Math.min(Math.max(opts.limit ?? 1000, 1), 5000);
  // dedicated + at least one open slot is not required; empty servers are useful listings too.
  const filter = `\\appid\\${appid}\\dedicated\\1`;
  const url = `https://api.steampowered.com/IGameServersService/GetServerList/v1/?key=${encodeURIComponent(opts.key)}&limit=${limit}&filter=${encodeURIComponent(filter)}`;
  const ctl = new AbortController();
  const t = setTimeout(() => ctl.abort(), opts.timeoutMs ?? 25_000);
  try {
    const res = await (opts.fetchImpl ?? fetch)(url, { signal: ctl.signal, headers: { accept: "application/json" } });
    if (!res.ok) throw new ValveFetchError(`Steam list answered HTTP ${res.status}`);
    return parseValveResponse(game, await res.json());
  } catch (e) {
    if (e instanceof ValveFetchError) throw e;
    // never echo the URL (it carries the API key)
    throw new ValveFetchError(e instanceof Error && e.name === "AbortError" ? "Steam list timed out" : "Steam list request failed");
  } finally {
    clearTimeout(t);
  }
}
import { db } from "@/lib/db";
import { getSettingBool } from "@/lib/settings";
import { nxeonConnectionKeys } from "@/lib/server-directory-data";
import { fetchValveList, VALVE_APPIDS, ValveFetchError, type ExternalCandidate } from "./valve";

/**
 * Ingest one game from the Steam master list into ExternalServer. Gated:
 * `apply` writes only when Setting directory_ingest_enabled is true. Dry run
 * (default) fetches + counts and writes nothing.
 *
 * Dedupe at the door: a candidate whose connection (host:port or ip:port)
 * equals something Nxeon hosts is dropped — the directory shows OUR entry
 * (with the Nxeon badge), not a duplicate. Candidates already stored under the
 * same connKey from another source row are skipped too. Rows not seen for
 * PRUNE_AFTER_DAYS are deleted so a dead server does not linger.
 */
export const PRUNE_AFTER_DAYS = 3;

export type IngestResult = { game: string; fetched: number; inserted: number; updated: number; duplicates: number; pruned: number; dryRun: boolean };

export function splitDuplicates<T extends { connKey: string; ipKey: string | null }>(cands: T[], nxeonKeys: Set<string>): { keep: T[]; dup: number } {
  const seen = new Set<string>();
  const keep: T[] = [];
  let dup = 0;
  for (const c of cands) {
    const keys = [c.connKey, ...(c.ipKey ? [c.ipKey] : [])];
    if (keys.some((k) => nxeonKeys.has(k) || seen.has(k))) { dup++; continue; }
    keys.forEach((k) => seen.add(k));
    keep.push(c);
  }
  return { keep, dup };
}

export async function ingestValveGame(game: string, opts: { apply: boolean; key: string; limit?: number; fetchImpl?: typeof fetch }): Promise<IngestResult> {
  if (!VALVE_APPIDS[game]) throw new Error(`Unsupported game for the Steam list: ${game}`);
  if (opts.apply && !(await getSettingBool("directory_ingest_enabled", false))) {
    throw new Error("Ingestion is switched off (Setting directory_ingest_enabled). Turn it on in /admin/directory first.");
  }
  const run = opts.apply ? await db.directoryIngestRun.create({ data: { source: "valve", game } }) : null;
  try {
    const fetched = await fetchValveList(game, { key: opts.key, limit: opts.limit, fetchImpl: opts.fetchImpl });
    const nxKeys = await nxeonConnectionKeys();
    const { keep, dup } = splitDuplicates<ExternalCandidate>(fetched, nxKeys);
    let inserted = 0, updated = 0, pruned = 0;
    if (opts.apply) {
      const existing = new Map((await db.externalServer.findMany({ where: { source: "valve", game }, select: { id: true, sourceKey: true } })).map((r) => [r.sourceKey, r.id]));
      const now = new Date();
      for (let i = 0; i < keep.length; i += 100) {
        await db.$transaction(keep.slice(i, i + 100).map((c) => {
          const data = {
            game: c.game, name: c.name, host: c.host, ip: c.ip, port: c.port, queryPort: c.queryPort, map: c.map,
            players: c.players, maxPlayers: c.maxPlayers, version: c.version, tags: c.tags,
            connKey: c.connKey, ipKey: c.ipKey, lastSeenAt: now,
          };
          if (existing.has(c.sourceKey)) updated++; else inserted++;
          return db.externalServer.upsert({
            where: { source_sourceKey: { source: "valve", sourceKey: c.sourceKey } },
            create: { source: "valve", sourceKey: c.sourceKey, ...data }, update: data,
          });
        }));
      }
      // Rows that now collide with something Nxeon hosts are removed (they were listed before we hosted them).
      const gone = await db.externalServer.deleteMany({
        where: { source: "valve", game, OR: [{ lastSeenAt: { lt: new Date(Date.now() - PRUNE_AFTER_DAYS * 86_400_000) } }, { connKey: { in: [...nxKeys] } }] },
      });
      pruned = gone.count;
      await db.directoryIngestRun.update({ where: { id: run!.id }, data: { finishedAt: new Date(), fetched: fetched.length, inserted, updated, duplicates: dup, pruned } });
    }
    return { game, fetched: fetched.length, inserted, updated, duplicates: dup, pruned, dryRun: !opts.apply };
  } catch (e) {
    const msg = e instanceof ValveFetchError ? e.message : e instanceof Error ? e.message : "ingest failed";
    if (run) await db.directoryIngestRun.update({ where: { id: run.id }, data: { finishedAt: new Date(), error: msg.slice(0, 300) } }).catch(() => {});
    throw e;
  }
}
